{{also|techno-}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From ''[[technology]]''.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|music genre}} A style of [[music]] characterized by repetitive instrumental music produced for use in a continuous DJ set. The central rhythmic component is most often in common time (4/4), where time is marked with a bass drum on each quarter note pulse, a backbeat played by snare or clap on the second and fourth pulses of the bar, and an open hi-hat sounding every second eighth note.

